From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: tsl2583: Accept a zero-padded LSCI record

The iPad mini 2's alsCalibration, which the bootloader copies into
apple,als-calibration, is 200 bytes: an LSCI v2 header giving a length
of 72, the 64-byte CT819 record, and 128 zero bytes. The driver wants
the header's length to be the property's, so it rejects the record and
the sensor reports uncalibrated lux.

Take the length from the header instead and accept a longer property
when the bytes after the record are all zero. The header, the 16-bit
word checksum over the record and the record checks stay as they were;
on a J85 the record's checksum is 0xffff and its values are in range.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c b/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c
index 809b54a..c39f91e 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@ static int apple_als_load_calibration(struct tsl2583_chip *chip)
 	struct device *dev = &chip->client->dev;
 	struct apple_als_calibration *cal = &chip->cal;
 	const u8 *record;
-	size_t len;
+	size_t len, rec_len;
 	u32 checksum = 0;
 	u8 *data;
 	int gain_index;
@@ -319,16 +319,28 @@ static int apple_als_load_calibration(struct tsl2583_chip *chip)
 				     "failed to read LSCI calibration\n");
 	}
 
-	if (len < APPLE_ALS_CAL_HEADER_SIZE + info->cal_record_size ||
-	    len & 1 || data[1] != info->cal_version || data[2] != 1 ||
+	/*
+	 * The header gives the record's length. The copy can be longer, padded
+	 * with zeros: the iPad mini 2's 200-byte alsCalibration holds a 72-byte
+	 * LSCI v2 record.
+	 */
+	if (len < APPLE_ALS_CAL_HEADER_SIZE + info->cal_record_size) {
+		dev_err(dev, "invalid LSCI v%u calibration header\n",
+			info->cal_version);
+		goto invalid;
+	}
+	rec_len = get_unaligned_le16(data + 4);
+	if (rec_len < APPLE_ALS_CAL_HEADER_SIZE + info->cal_record_size ||
+	    rec_len > len || rec_len & 1 ||
+	    data[1] != info->cal_version || data[2] != 1 ||
 	    data[3] != APPLE_ALS_CAL_HEADER_SIZE ||
-	    get_unaligned_le16(data + 4) != len) {
+	    memchr_inv(data + rec_len, 0, len - rec_len)) {
 		dev_err(dev, "invalid LSCI v%u calibration header\n",
 			info->cal_version);
 		goto invalid;
 	}
 
-	for (i = 0; i < len; i += 2)
+	for (i = 0; i < rec_len; i += 2)
 		checksum += get_unaligned_le16(data + i);
 	if ((u16)checksum != U16_MAX) {
 		dev_err(dev, "invalid LSCI calibration checksum\n");
